# Keep the frozen dataset byte-identical across machines.
#
# Git normalises line endings by default (LF in the repo, CRLF on Windows
# checkout). For a dataset that exists specifically so every member works on
# IDENTICAL bytes, that conversion defeats the purpose: a teammate on macOS or
# Linux would check out different bytes than Ming committed, and any checksum
# we quote in the report would not reproduce.
#
# -text disables all conversion: what was committed is what is checked out.
data/raw/*.csv        -text
data/raw/*.txt        -text
data/processed/*.parquet binary
